  "notes": [
    {
      "row": "notes",
      "title": "3.8 vs 3.5: the same architecture",
      "text": "Qwen3.8-27B and Qwen3.5-27B have identical hidden size, layer count, head counts, layer_types and rope. The config deltas are output_gate_type \"swish\", an explicit partial_rotary_factor, untied embeddings and a newer tokenizer. A newer train and a newer schema — not a new model.",
      "code": [
        {
          "role": "definition",
          "src": "qwen35.hf",
          "lines": [
            761,
            771
          ],
          "expect": {
            "symbol": "Qwen3_5DecoderLayer.__init__",
            "first": "def __init__(self, config: Qwen3_5TextConfig, layer_idx: int):",
            "sha": "b127835a",
            "span": [
              761,
              771
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "row": "notes",
      "title": "Why the memory profile is unlike Gemma's",
      "text": "Gemma bounds its cache with a sliding window — still a cache, just shorter. Here 48 of 64 layers have NO key/value cache at all: they carry a fixed-size recurrent state plus a 4-wide conv state, whatever the context length. Only the 16 full layers cache anything that grows.",
      "code": [
        {
          "role": "definition",
          "src": "qwen35.hf",
          "lines": [
            441,
            463
